From: PyDevices usbif
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shared/tinyusb: add a tusb_config.h extension hook

Purpose: let a user C module (usbif) enable additional TinyUSB class
drivers (CFG_TUD_AUDIO, later CFG_TUD_VIDEO) and define their sizing
macros in a header it owns, named via MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_TUSB_CONFIG
from the module's build glue. Keeps the diff against MicroPython to
these seven lines; all volatile class configuration lives in usbif.

Provenance: written for usbif Phase 0 (Spike B), 2026-08-29.
Upstream-version range: authored against v1.28.0. Checked against
master the same day: the file tail above the hook has already been
restructured upstream (USBD_EP_BUILTIN_MAX is now computed; CFG_TUD_NCM
added), so this hunk deliberately anchors only on the two trailing
endif lines, which are unchanged from v1.28.0 through current master.
Order: first and only patch in the series.
Test: build ESP32_GENERIC_S3 with MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_TUSB_CONFIG
pointing at a header enabling CFG_TUD_AUDIO with stub sizing; firmware
must build and, with no descriptor changes, behave identically
(pending — the build half of Spike B).

--- a/shared/tinyusb/tusb_config.h
+++ b/shared/tinyusb/tusb_config.h
@@ -147,3 +147,10 @@
+// Allow a user C module to extend this configuration with additional TinyUSB
+// class drivers (e.g. CFG_TUD_AUDIO) and their sizing macros, without editing
+// this file. The named header is supplied by the module's build glue.
+#ifdef MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_TUSB_CONFIG
+#include MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_TUSB_CONFIG
+#endif
+
 #endif // MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_USBDEV

 #endif // MICROPY_INCLUDED_SHARED_TINYUSB_TUSB_CONFIG_H
